MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The smaller stainless hose clamps felt useful because I have bought both an assortment of hose clamps and larger duct clamps; they serve a familiar fastening purpose in a different size.",
    "The small Gorilla epoxy felt like a natural choice because I have used Gorilla tape and vinyl cement, and a small amount of quick-setting adhesive fits that practical repair interest."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The cutting wheels and wire cup brush assume a metalworking task and compatible tools that my purchases do not establish.",
    "The specific pipe fitting and nut sizes would need to match an actual repair. Likewise, electronic cleaner, wet-area putty, and a two-pack of steel-reinforced epoxy are only useful to me when the relevant job comes up."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My repair supplies seem to have been taken as a reason to suggest almost any workshop consumable, even when it serves a different task.",
    "Buying hose clamps seems to have been stretched into an interest in specific plumbing fittings, although fastening a hose does not tell you which threaded connection I need."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The repeated hose-clamp purchases are a clearer sign of an ongoing need than my isolated purchases of other repair supplies.",
    "An item can fit my repair interests without being something I would choose now; size, quantity, intended material, and whether I have a matching task matter."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The suggestions recognized my interest in practical fastening and adhesives but assumed too many specific repair needs from that broader interest."
}
